    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ecdbdb1_399da338",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4487,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T19:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SVID discovery state isn\u0027t checked by pe_do_port_discovery_run().  Won\u0027t pe_do_discovery_run() send another Discover SVID?  It should probably be harmless to resend Discover SVID, but probably not the desired behavior.\n\nI supposed, this is temporary, because PE_DO_PORT_DISCOVERY will eventually be eliminated, correct?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4487,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4487,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "1fb45cd9f413fe759c90246d2af8c2e9737ac0bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a2c2836_34b4858f",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4487,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T19:40:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PE_DO_PORT_DISCOVERY has its own discovery state (basically) in the form of pe[port].vdm_cmd. As a temporary compatibility measure, this code sets that field after discovery. pe_vdm_request_run handles VDM-related flags, which are the other way that PE_DO_PORT_DISCOVERY is controlled.",
      "parentUuid": "6ecdbdb1_399da338",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4487,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4487,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "1fb45cd9f413fe759c90246d2af8c2e9737ac0bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75e615f6_2e7f9dca",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4487,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T19:58:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on traces I\u0027ve seen so far, we\u0027ll double-discover on NAKs (usually it\u0027s discover identity being NAK\u0027d), but that seems like an acceptable transition behavior as the ultimate goal is to align our states with the spec (which doesn\u0027t contain DO_PORT_DISCOVERY)",
      "parentUuid": "7a2c2836_34b4858f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4487,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4487,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "1fb45cd9f413fe759c90246d2af8c2e9737ac0bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "affc3a2d_f1c98e31",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4498,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T19:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The set state at line 4510 will ensure pe_attempt_port_discover() is called again, which is already using discover_port_identity_timer.  So I think you can safely reuse the same timer here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4493,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4498,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1fb45cd9f413fe759c90246d2af8c2e9737ac0bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09038d57_e14c3e3e",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4498,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T19:58:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should be safe to re-use the timer.  The timer\u0027s \"official\" use is to space out cable discovery.  Past that point, might as well put it to an additional use spacing BUSY responses.\n\nWe might want a configured maximum busy limit, but that would probably be a policy TODO for later",
      "parentUuid": "affc3a2d_f1c98e31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4493,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4498,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1fb45cd9f413fe759c90246d2af8c2e9737ac0bc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf66bae2_95429971",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4498,
